# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Summit Sensory Gym CPQ project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Modified**: `package.json`
  - Added `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1` to dependencies

### 2. Lock File Updated
- **Modified**: `package-lock.json`
  - Updated with @vercel/analytics package and all its dependencies (458 packages added)

### 3. Analytics Integration
- **Modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag in the root layout
  - This follows the official Next.js App Router pattern from Vercel's documentation

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide (fetched on 2026-07-12):
- Used Next.js App Router specific import path: `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout for application-wide tracking
- Positioned the component at the end of the body tag to avoid affecting page rendering

## Framework Context

- **Framework**: Next.js 16.2.10 with App Router
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Installation Location**: Root layout (`src/app/layout.tsx`)

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully - no compilation errors
✅ TypeScript type checking passed
✅ ESLint check passed for layout.tsx (no new linting errors introduced)
✅ Package lock file updated correctly

## Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Enable Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard by navigating to the Analytics section
2. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify analytics are working by checking the browser's Network tab for a fetch request from `/<unique-path>/view`
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

## Notes

- The Analytics component will only collect data when deployed on Vercel
- In local development, the component renders but doesn't send analytics data
- No additional configuration is required for basic page view tracking
- Custom events can be added later if needed using the Analytics SDK
